{title: Show Myself to Him}
{subtitle: John 14:21}
{key: Gm}
{tempo: 75}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Gm] | [Gm] | [Ebmaj7] | [Cm7] | ×2
| [Gm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
I will not leave you as [Ebmaj7]orphans behind
[Cm7]I am coming to you, [Gm]the truth defined
In a little while the world will [Ebmaj7]fade
But you will [Cm7]see me in the [Gm]shade
Because [Ebmaj7]I live, you also will [Gm]live
[Ebmaj7]This is the gift we [D]must give
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Whoever [Gm]holds to my commandments
And [Ebmaj7]keeps them with their own life
Is [Cm7]the one who loves me truly
And loves [Gm]me with the truth
Loved by my Father, I will love [Ebmaj7]him
[Cm7]And show myself to [Gm]him
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
On that day you will [Ebmaj7]know it's true
[Cm7]I am in my Father [Gm]for you
You are in me, [Ebmaj7]I am in you
[Cm7]This is the bond that stands [Gm]so new
Judas asked why [Ebmaj7]not the world
[Cm7]Jesus spoke the word un[Gm]furled
If anyone loves me, [Ebmaj7]keep the word
[Cm7]Make our home with you, [D]my lord
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Whoever [Gm]holds to my commandments
And [Ebmaj7]keeps them with their own life
Is [Cm7]the one who loves me truly
And loves [Gm]me with the truth
Loved by my Father, I will love [Ebmaj7]him
[Cm7]And show myself to [Gm]you
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]Whoever does not love [Gm]me
[Eb]Does not keep my [Gm]words to see
[Eb]The word you hear is not [Gm]my own
[Cm7]But the Father's who [D]has sown
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Show myself to [Gm]him
[Ebmaj7]Show myself to [Cm7]him
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [Cm7] | [Gm] | [Gm] | [Ebmaj7] | ×4
| [Cm7] | [Gm] |
